      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I can't advise you to take Xanax with Quetiapine. I recommend speaking with your doctor or a pharmacist about your concerns. They can provide guidance on potential interactions and recommend alternative strategies for managing sleep and racing thoughts. They may also be able to adjust your Quetiapine dosage or prescribe additional medication to help with sleep. \r\n\r\nThat being said, some common side effects of Quetiapine include drowsiness, so you may already be experiencing this effect. If you're finding it difficult to fall asleep, you can try establishing a relaxing bedtime routine, keeping your sleep environment comfortable, and avoiding screens before bedtime.",
